@host = http://localhost:5165

# The demo clinic, from:
#   dotnet run --project DYS.Molargo.API -- seed --demo
#
# The same clinic and the same credentials the desktop app seeds. Other users on it:
# cbrennan (reception), jellery (dentist), hito (hygienist) — all with the same password.

### Sign in. Everything below needs the token this returns.
# @name signIn
POST {{host}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clinicCode": "molargo-dental",
  "username": "rvance",
  "password": "molargo-demo"
}

### What the token says about the caller — tenant, provider, role, permissions.
@token = {{signIn.response.body.token}}

GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Patients at this clinic. The tenant filter is on the context, not on this query.
GET {{host}}/patients?page=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Searched.
GET {{host}}/patients?search=yuen
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One patient.
GET {{host}}/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create one.
POST {{host}}/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Patient",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-04-12",
  "mobile": "0400 000 000",
  "email": "test@example.test"
}

### Appointments. No range means the coming month — see the endpoint's note.
GET {{host}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A specific window.
GET {{host}}/appointments?from=2026-09-01&to=2026-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A course of treatment and its visits, in treatment order.
GET {{host}}/appointments/series/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token — should be 401, not an empty list.
GET {{host}}/patients
